Test-only patch: plan Section 22 boundary cases of the Phase 2 targets that no upstream test
covers (plan step S34; human decision H3, follow-up of 2026-11-24)

Applies to: the copy of upstream origin/main 7caec762799bece6fba38e4298b8ca7db8bac12c after
01-request-state-wire.patch (scripts/apply-patches.sh applies formal/trusted/patches/*.patch in
file-name order, patch -p1 -F 0, only to the copy in .llbc/work/; the real source is never
patched). Files: crates/rmcp/src/model.rs, crates/rmcp/src/model/task.rs,
crates/rmcp/src/transport/async_rw.rs, crates/rmcp/src/transport/auth.rs,
crates/rmcp/src/transport/common/client_side_sse.rs,
crates/rmcp/src/transport/streamable_http_server/tower.rs. Generated with git diff in a scratch
git repository holding the patch-01 copy (one hunk per file, at its end). The patch body below
is the authoritative content.

Change: #[cfg(test)] code only. Every added line lies inside a #[cfg(test)] module: at the end
of the existing test module of model.rs, model/task.rs, async_rw.rs (mod test), auth.rs and
client_side_sse.rs, and in a new #[cfg(test)] mod phase2_boundary_tests at the end of tower.rs
(its added lines are one blank separator line, the #[cfg(test)] and mod lines, and the module
body, comments included).
No non-test line, no dependency, no Cargo.toml change; no existing line is removed or changed.
The added tests are named s34_<id>_<case>; each cites its plan Section 22 row and the Lean
theorem it mirrors. Their expected values are taken from the signed-off Lean statements and
the Defs they use (Defs.parseI64, Defs.Tower.defaultPort, Defs.Methods lists, Defs.Sse model
and checks, Defs.Net definitions and checks), not from running the code. They call the
targets directly (M06/M07 pub(crate), T01-T08 and A01-A03 private: reachable only from
in-module tests), so they run in the translated feature configuration plus macros, without
transport-streamable-http-client-reqwest. A test of a feature-gated item carries the item's cfg:
the M06 test #[cfg(any(feature = "client", feature = "server"))] and the four M07 tests
#[cfg(feature = "client")], as numeric_string_value and matches_response_id (model.rs lines
321 and 329 at 7caec76); every other test calls an ungated item or lies in a module gated
already (transport/: client or server; async_rw, auth, client_side_sse, tower: their features).
So the crate's tests compile with any feature set, e.g. request-state alone (the Phase 1
evidence command). The limiter tests build every start state field by field, never through
SseEventSizeLimiter::new, which no signed-off statement covers.

Why (plan Section 19, "Tests (human decision H3)"; Section 21, H3): new Rust tests of these
functions must live in SDK *.rs files, which stay byte-identical to upstream. The S34
upstream-test map (formal/trusted/evidence/README.md) found 96 uncovered and 8 partial plan
Section 22 cases; this patch covers them. A test-only patch is a process exception
(VERIFICATION.md Section 4 defines translation patches as behaviour-preserving edits that make
an item translate); plan Section 21 (H3) asks for it to be recorded in formal/docs/STATUS.md,
"Documents", as a further deviation from VERIFICATION.md.

Effect on the translation: none. Charon does not compile #[cfg(test)] items, and every hunk is
at the end of its file, so no translated item moves (the Source: lines of
formal/translation/ are unchanged); checked by translating the copy with both patches and
comparing it byte for byte with formal/translation/ (formal/trusted/evidence/README.md, S34).

Evidence in CI: patched-tests.yml runs cargo test --locked --lib on the copy with both patches
(translated features plus macros, overflow checks and debug assertions on), which runs these
tests. Delete this patch if the tests land in the SDK source.
